const canonical = "https://samedayappliance.repair/services/refrigerator-repair/how-long-do-refrigerators-last/";

const title = "How Long Do Refrigerators Last? Lifespan Guide";
const description = "Most refrigerators last 10 to 15 years, with premium built-ins going 20+. What shortens the life, the warning signs, and when repair beats replacement.";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "How long does a refrigerator last on average?",
    a: "Most standard refrigerators last 10 to 15 years, with the industry average landing around 13. Compact and mini fridges tend to run shorter, closer to 8 to 10 years, while premium built-ins like Sub-Zero regularly reach 20 years or more because the cabinet outlives the serviceable parts by decades. Where a specific unit lands depends far more on maintenance and installation conditions than on the badge."
  },
  {
    q: "What makes a refrigerator wear out faster?",
    a: "The biggest factor is condenser coils that never get cleaned. Packed with dust and pet hair, they trap heat and force the compressor to work harder for years, which is what actually kills most units early. Other accelerants are poor ventilation (a fridge crammed into a tight cabinet), frequent power interruptions, a garage or unconditioned space in the heat, and coastal salt air, which is why we see faster motor wear in beach cities. Cleaning the coils once or twice a year is the single best thing you can do."
  },
  {
    q: "What are the signs a refrigerator is near the end?",
    a: "Food spoiling faster than it should, a compressor that runs constantly and never cycles off, heavy condensation or frost buildup, the motor feeling hot to the touch, and rising energy bills. One of these alone is usually a repair. Several at once on a unit past year 12, especially with a major part failure, is when replacement starts to make sense."
  },
  {
    q: "Is it worth repairing a 10-year-old refrigerator?",
    a: "Usually yes. A 10-year-old fridge is mid-life for most models, and common repairs like a fan motor, defrost part, or damper run $260 to $460 without touching the sealed system. The math only tilts toward replacement when a mid-tier unit past year 12 needs a major sealed-system repair such as a compressor. Premium and ultra-premium units are worth repairing well past year 15. Our techs give you the number and the honest call on-site."
  },
  {
    q: "Does brand matter for how long a fridge lasts?",
    a: "Less than people think. Build tier matters more than brand name. An ultra-premium built-in has a heavier cabinet and serviceable components designed to be replaced, so it lasts decades. A budget top-freezer will run its 10 to 13 years regardless of the logo if the coils are kept clean. The fastest way to shorten any fridge, at any price, is to never clean the condenser and to crowd it into a hot, unventilated space."
  }
];

